      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This would be really great if implemented. \n\nMy group is a sleep group, and we get two types of people we want to warn. \n\n1. People deliberately being trolls and trying to wake people up/yelling.\n\n2. People who are oblivious to the fact that there are legitimately people trying to sleep, and are practically yelling into their mic talking to a friend or on the phone or something like that.\n\nIn case one, I honestly just kick/ban them instantly, they know what they are doing and aren't going to stop for a warning. But in case two some amount of those people might learn some self awareness if the warning is directed. As of now, most shrug it off, or don't understand why they were warned. To quote one person I warned then had to kick this morning, \"VRCHAT BUGGING\" screamed out in the middle of a bunch of asleep people, followed by more equally loud talking.\n\nIn other environments this could be supplemented with the warner directly talking to the person, but in my experience that is significantly harder than it sounds. Trying to talk over someone practically screaming and not caring about anyone outside of their little bubble is a real challenge. For example, I attempted this in the above quoted example, and could not manage to get their attention.\n\nI also believe this could help mitigate another issue, which is that almost everyone I have warned has thought the warning is coming from \"vrchat\" or a \"vrchat moderator\" rather than a group moderator. Which, while great for protecting players from blowback, it might not the most healthy thing for the platform. I would hate to see such a useful tool be removed because of this.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-05-31T16:47:04.123Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "(Reposting from feature requests)\n\nCurrently, when we use the \"Warn User\" button in VRChat, a generic message is sent stating \"You have been warned for your behavior.\"\n\nHowever, I believe it would greatly enhance the user experience if we were able to provide a specific reason for the warning. By including a customized explanation, such as \"A moderator has sent you a warning: Please refrain from micspamming,\" the user would immediately understand what they have done wrong, allowing for clearer communication.",
